cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FontVibe Rune Transliterator"
message: "If you use these rune tables or this library, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "FontVibe"
    website: "https://fontvibe.ai"
abstract: >-
  Phonetic transliteration of English and other Latin-alphabet text into
  Elder Futhark (24 runes), Younger Futhark long-branch (16 runes) and
  Anglo-Saxon Futhorc (32 runes), and back. Shared JSON mapping tables drive
  dependency-free JavaScript and Python implementations whose output is
  verified against golden data recorded from the implementation behind
  fontvibe.ai's rune tools, across every Unicode scalar value. A phonetic
  approximation, not a translation into Old Norse or Old English.
keywords:
  - runes
  - runic
  - futhark
  - elder futhark
  - younger futhark
  - futhorc
  - anglo-saxon runes
  - transliteration
  - unicode
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://fontvibe.ai/tools/rune-generator"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Funovate-Technology/fontvibe-runes"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
